# 16. Every Failed Experiment Is Useful

A failed experiment must produce information.

Do NOT simply write:

> "It doesn't work."

Record:

```text
Hypothesis
Experiment
Environment
Expected result
Actual result
Logs
Failure reason
What was learned
Next experiment
```

Example:

```text
Hypothesis:
Vulkan FP16 GEMM can accelerate the attention projection.

Result:
Kernel executes successfully but is slower than NEON.

Conclusion:
GPU dispatch overhead dominates for this tensor size.

Next:
Benchmark larger tensor sizes and investigate kernel fusion.
```

This is valuable engineering progress.

