# 21. MVP First, Perfection Later

Do NOT spend weeks trying to build:

* perfect compiler infrastructure
* perfect NPU support
* perfect GPU kernels
* perfect expert scheduler
* perfect memory manager

before Waqti can actually perform a coding task.

The minimum useful loop is:

```text
User
 ↓
Waqti
 ↓
Model
 ↓
Understand task
 ↓
Inspect repository
 ↓
Modify code
 ↓
Build
 ↓
Observe failure
 ↓
Fix
 ↓
Build again
 ↓
Success
```

Get this working first.

Then optimize the runtime underneath it.

---

# 22. Definition of "Working"

Waqti MVP is considered real only when it can demonstrate:

1. Load a real model.
2. Generate a response.
3. Stream output.
4. Execute at least one tool.
5. Read a file.
6. Modify a file.
7. Run a build/test command.
8. Read the resulting error.
9. Make a correction.
10. Successfully complete a small coding task.

A screenshot of an app UI is NOT sufficient.

A successful model load is NOT sufficient.

A benchmark without agent functionality is NOT sufficient.

The target is an actual end-to-end coding-agent loop.

